{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":12862847,"ns":0,"title":"Neostenanthera neurosericea","revisions":[{"revid":1371756757,"parentid":1359946598,"minor":true,"timestamp":"2026-08-28T07:18:54Z","size":2667,"sha1":"d881bac70843c51133b88e870dadb2300fd52019","slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","content":"{{Short description|Genus of flowering plants}}\n{{speciesbox\n|status = DD\n|status_system = IUCN3.1\n|status_ref = <ref name=iucn>{{cite iucn |author=Cosiaux, A. |author2=Couvreur, T.L.P. |author3=Erkens, R.H.J. |year=2019 |title=''Neostenanthera neurosericea'' |volume=2019 |article-number=e.T133040073A133042999 |doi=10.2305/IUCN.UK.2019-3.RLTS.T133040073A133042999.en |language=en |access-date=18 June 2026}}</ref>\n|genus = Neostenanthera\n|species = neurosericea\n|authority = ([[Ludwig Diels|Diels]]) [[Arthur Wallis Exell|Exell]] (1935)\n|synonyms =\n*''Boutiquea platypetala'' {{small|([[Heinrich Gustav Adolf Engler|Engl.]] & Diels) Le Thomas (1965)}}\n*''Neostenanthera macrantha'' {{small|(Mildbr. & Diels) Exell (1935)}}\n*''Neostenanthera platypetala'' {{small|(Engl. & Diels) Pellegr. (1950)}}\n*''Stenanthera macrantha'' {{small|Mildbr. & Diels (1915)}}\n*''Stenanthera neurosericea'' {{small|Diels (1907)}}\n*''Stenanthera platypetala'' {{small|Engl. & Diels (1907)}}\n|synonyms_ref = <ref name = powo>[https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:74180-1 ''Neostenanthera neurosericea'' (Diels) Exell]. ''[[Plants of the World Online]]''. Retrieved 3 June 2024.</ref>\n}}\n\n'''''Neostenanthera neurosericea''''' is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Annonaceae]]. It is a shrub or tree native to southwestern [[Cameroon]] and [[Gabon]].<ref name = powo/>\n\nThis plant is known to science by only 14 specimens collected from eight locations. It is a [[shrub]] or tree generally growing {{convert|3|to|5|m|ft|0}} tall, sometimes reaching {{convert|10|m|ft}}. It has showy flowers and fruits. Its pollen is shed as permanent tetrads.<ref name=\"GuoTang2017\">{{cite journal|last1=Guo|first1=Xing|last2=Tang|first2=Chin Cheung|last3=Thomas|first3=Daniel C.|last4=Couvreur|first4=Thomas L. P.|last5=Saunders|first5=Richard M. K.|title=A mega-phylogeny of the Annonaceae: taxonomic placement of five enigmatic genera and support for a new tribe, Phoenicantheae|journal=Scientific Reports|volume=7|issue=1|year=2017|page=7323|issn=2045-2322|doi=10.1038/s41598-017-07252-2|doi-access=free|pmc=5544705|pmid=28779135}}</ref> It grows in evergreen forest habitat.<ref name=iucn/>\n\nThis is a vulnerable species threatened by habitat loss as forest is cleared for agriculture.<ref name=iucn/>\n\n==References==\n{{Reflist}}\n\n{{Taxonbar|from=Q15363782|from2=Q4950462}}\n\n[[Category:Neostenanthera|neurosericea]]\n[[Category:Flora of Cameroon]]\n[[Category:Flora of Gabon]]\n[[Category:Data deficient flora of Africa]]\n[[Category:Plants described in 1907]]\n[[Category:Taxa named by Ludwig Diels]]\n[[Category:Taxonomy articles created by Polbot]]\n\n{{Annonaceae-stub}}"}}}],"contentmodel":"wikitext","pagelanguage":"en","pagelanguagehtmlcode":"en","pagelanguagedir":"ltr","touched":"2026-10-26T19:32:56Z","lastrevid":1371756757,"length":2667}]}}